ant you to be exactly  who you want you to be it's a  documentary that I saw at Sundance and  it ended up being one of my favorites  it's told by master documentarian  two-time Oscar winner Barbara Kopple  and it tells the story of GG gorgeous  who is a transgender YouTube star it's  expertly put together and really  inspiring I teared up quite a lot  watching this film because I cannot  imagine what it must be like to not feel  like you are the gender that you were  born in and also how incredibly tough it  must be to navigate that road the thing  that makes it so inspiring is that Gigi  is completely herself and damn anyone  who doesn't agree with her and it is  always so great to see someone living an  authentic life this is everything Gigi  gorgeous is out in New York and LA this  weekend and then on YouTube read on  February 8th I was scared  but I was happy I was the real meat  having Gigi happy is way more important  than me having old Gregg  so just to recap my ultimate picks this  week would be the salesman I am NOT your  negro and this is everything new GG  gorgeous in theaters each of these films  speak about an issue that is very  important right now and each of these  films are well worth your time and money  I know it's tough when I talk about  these films and you can't actually see  them but just try to write them down  because hopefully at one point or  another you will get to I'm Alicia  Malone you can follow me on Twitter at  Alicia Malone and I'll see you next week

